description: The browser rows depend on `local-scripts/coi-serve.py`, a file outside the repo, so they cannot run on a machine that lacks it, and they take the node-host and wasmtime checks down with them.
 
 What I see on my machine (no `local-scripts/` beside the checkout, `LW_BROWSER_TOOLS` unset):
 
 - `checks/browser-boot.sh` (P4.0, P4.1, P6.4) stops with "FAIL: server on <port> did not start". Its node-host and wasmtime rows come after the browser block, and `wait_up` exits, so those never run either, though neither needs a browser or COOP/COEP.
 - `checks/lane5.sh` (P4.2), `checks/eval-hosts.sh` (P7.5) and `checks/size-boot-legmacs.sh` start the same server.
 - The result is identical on main and on every branch I gated, so no branch currently has a passing result for these rows here.
 
 The script only serves a directory with the two COOP/COEP headers (`SharedArrayBuffer` for the stock lane's key ring).
 
 Proposed fix: fall through instead of failing hard.
 
 1. When the COI server or Chromium is unavailable, the browser lanes report SKIP with the reason and the script goes on, so node-host and wasmtime still run and decide the row. A row left with nothing but skipped lanes (P4.2, P7.5) exits 2, which the gate already counts as not passed, so a skip never reads as green.
 2. Put the COI server in the repo (a few lines on node, which the hosts already need), and have the four scripts use it by default, with `LW_BROWSER_TOOLS` as an override.
